/workspace/shared/research/re_production.md:52:The aggregate log intentionally drops coordinates, so a separate raw-action audit was made on 10 replay trajectories per team. Coordinates are farm `(row,column)` before the action; crop/land geometry is stable enough to infer blocks, but exact within-block tile order is not invariant across episodes.
/workspace/shared/research/re_production.md:61:For example, in the 10-replay Boey audit d6 plant actions at `(7:9,1:4)` are overwhelmingly STRAWBERRY (136 S versus 14 M and 48 W total that day), while d8 actions in the lower-left block are 90 W. M&M&P&Q is still clearer (d6: 150 S; d8: 137 W). This gives a usable first layout rule for top-RE: allocate the second unlocked quadrant to berry production and third to wheat for the M&M&P&Q/DSM/Boey family; fuxi requires its own mixed-block policy. Do not hard-code a coordinate ordering within a block yet.
