/workspace/shared/research/re_production.md:36:At herd size 10+, mean units/turn are WATER 1.59, HARVEST .78, CARE .70, FEED .72, COLLECT_FERTILIZER .72 and FERTILIZE .32 (61,219 turns). With no animals all seven production operations are exactly zero (341 turns); at 1–9 animals, service counts are only about .22–.23. This supports scaling animal service with herd and WATER/HARVEST with the crop base. CARE+FEED occur together on only 35.6% of turns containing either; CARE+COLLECT on 26.9%, so a clone must route individual workers rather than bind a three-op triplet.
/workspace/shared/research/re_production.md:48:Calendar phase captures much of the aggregate decision but is not a playable clone: next step is raw target/path reconstruction and state-bucket residuals (ripe/water need, animal status, carried fertilizer).
/workspace/shared/research/re_production.md:93:Calendar presence generalises, but exact WATER is only 46.7%, reinforcing that raw path/state reconstruction is needed before calling this a clone.
/workspace/shared/research/bcppo_design_codex.md:9:Не тратить первый день на полный autoregressive transformer. Минимальная правильная версия: target как navigation prior; затем сэмплировать допустимое направление с log-prob/entropy, либо в target — non-move op. После этого нужен sequential allocator farmer→hands для seeds/shed/inventory. Рынок лучше декодировать последовательно в 10 slots с состоянием money/shed/seeds/land/hires и STOP; временный компромисс — маскировать qty и считать likelihood только реально посланных orders.
