/workspace/shared/research/bcppo_v3_design_codex.md:48:There is a second kernel-launch-heavy path in **`policy.py:127-144`**: Python loop over up to 17 units, with nested 5-crop and 12-item loops, clone/mask/scatter/Categorical calls per unit.  This is especially unfriendly to `torch.compile` because `U_eff=int(...)` creates a dynamic host scalar.
/workspace/shared/research/bcppo_v3_design_codex.md:61:**As data augmentation / a candidate initialisation: yes, conditionally.  As an assumed strong GPU league opponent: no, not until rollout-gated.**  `es3_g5` is a structured tape/replay controller plus repair layers.  On expert trajectories BC can learn its local actions, but a single unit/board action error changes positions and inventory; then the clone visits states absent from the teacher distribution.  The present BC state is also not a full controller state: `gpufeat.py:23-34` retains only whether YARN was among the first two shops, not the full route/tape history.  If es3 decisions distinguish histories collapsed by these features, supervised labels are irreducibly multimodal and high teacher-forced accuracy will overstate closed-loop competence.
